# ESX team manifest

| Role | Duty | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Arch | Coordinate scope, evidence, review, records and communication | Main session |
| Bob | Implement and maintain code/docs within agreed invariants | Scientific/software implementation |
| Richard | Independent review and independently selected check | Required scientific acceptance |
| Scout | Find bounded source, dataset or artifact evidence | Owner/location uncertainty |
| Prober | Construct/reduce numerical or statistical witnesses | Decisive claim needs measurement |
| Bisector | Locate a reproducible historical boundary | Good/bad endpoints and frozen predicate exist |
| Auditor | Check policy, contracts and evidence tooling | Substantial cross-contract change or conflict |

Role files in ../agents own tools and role-specific duties. Every role preloads
only `esx-common`; other procedures have explicit Read paths. No model is pinned:
the runtime inherits the configured model until the owner chooses per-role models.
Runtime availability, tool permissions and resume support require a deployment
smoke check. A role name alone does not prove independent execution.

The authority is [ARCHITECT.md](ARCHITECT.md). Contracts live under devel-loop;
mechanisms live under tools/esx. Project-specific science belongs in esx/project_profile.md.
